==== Flash Layout ====
Please read the article [[docs:techref:flash.layout]] for a better understanding. It contains a couple of explanations. Then let's have a quick view at flash layout of this particular device:

^   GL.iNet GL-MT300N Flash Layout  ^^^^^^^^
^ Layer0 |  w25q128 16 MiB  |||||||
^ Layer1 |  **mtd0** \\ ''u-boot'' \\ 192 KiB  |  **mtd1** \\ ''u-boot-env'' \\ 64 KiB  |  **mtd2** \\ ''factory'' \\ 64 KiB  |  **mtd3** \\ ''firmware'' \\ 15872 KiB  |||  **mtd7** \\ ''art'' \\ 64 KiB  |
^ Layer2 | | | |  **mtd4** \\ ''kernel'' \\ about 1.2 MiB  |  **mtd5** \\ ''rootfs''  || |
^ <color magenta>mountpoint</color> | | | | |  ''/''  || |
^ filesystem | | | | |  [[docs:techref:filesystems#overlayfs|overlayfs]]  || |
^ Layer3 | | | | |  **''/dev/root''** \\ about 6.0 MiB  |  **mtd6** \\ ''rootfs_data'' \\ 8.5 MiB  | |
^ <color magenta>mountpoint</color> |  //none//  |  //none//  |  //none//  |  //none//  |  ''/rom''  |  ''/overlay''  |  //none//  |
^ filesystem |  //none//  |  //none//  |  //none//  |  //none//  |  [[docs:techref:filesystems#SquashFS]]  |  [[docs:techref:filesystems#JFFS2]]  |  //none//  |

Note the "art" partition with the SoC specific Wifi data.

